A||||5||mrgone||cleaning the engine||||1||
Z||000000||mrgone||05-06-2001||11:48 PM||||mine is cosmetically dirty. can i hose it down? should the engine be running?<P>powerwashing a bad idea?||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||05-07-2001||12:59 AM||||I always wash mine while it is running (but not too hot).  I use the pressure washer thingy at the self serve car wash.  As long as it is running you'll know where not to spray water (if it starts to stumble or die then you hit something important).||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||05-07-2001||07:22 AM||||just stay away as much as possible from directly spraying distributor, relays at top of firewall and by battery. Make sure the pressure dont blow off any vacum lines. Im also carfull not to spray area around map and tps sensor hard or around the openings in alternator.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||05-07-2001||09:36 AM||||I'd be careful about spraying hot exhaust manifolds. Seems like the one on my coupe cracked at about the same time I pressure washed it. <BR>Could be a coincidence...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000004||RacinRob||05-07-2001||10:48 AM||||I've hosed mine off a bunch of times.  I just used the water pressure of a hose and a small sprayer thingy.  I just soaked the engine compartment in degreaser first, I've done it hot and cool (the engine) and it seems to work better hot.||||reg||1
Z||000005||84Bill||05-07-2001||01:14 PM||||Always clean my engines cold. Then fire them up and take a spin to dry her out. Every so often she fusses after a bath but no long term bad things have ever resulted. Check out my 88 Engine on my page. She be very clean <BR> <A HREF="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/fiero</A> ||||reg||1
